      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should I check on a supplier's certificate?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Three things: that it has not expired, that the manufacturer and site named on it match the factory producing your order, and that the product it describes is the product you are buying. Most certification problems are visible on the certificate itself."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you verify sterilisation and biocompatibility?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Where ethylene oxide sterilisation is used, residual limits and validation matter, and ISO 10993 biocompatibility evidence should be appropriate to the contact type and duration."
